logic malignancy", "Metabolic encephalopathy: Mild ataxia and visual changes might imply metabolic derangement, but labs show normal electrolytes, glucose, and calcium", "Neurologic autoimmune process: Blurry vision and ataxia could suggest autoimmune etiology, but systemic constitutional symptoms with blasts make this less likely"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional B symptoms (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Pancytopenia with blast cells", "New neurological symptoms (visual changes, ataxia)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.4582123522454169, "posterior": 0.5818264641096298, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Blasts in peripheral blood decisively exclude reactive leukocytosis (B5), which cannot explain blast proliferation. This confirms a malignant process (AML/ALL)…"], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.041, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Pancytopenia is inconsistent with ALL's typical leukocytosis, directly weakening B2 as a diagnosis."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.005, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The subacute phase and lack of chronic CML features (like splenomegaly) strongly support B1 over B3. Chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms rarely present with s…"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cel