a (hemoglobin 10 g/dL, platelets 109,000/mm³) contradict ALL (B2), which typically causes leukocytosis rather than cytopenias?", "summary": "Pancytopenia is inconsistent with ALL's typical leukocytosis, directly weakening B2 as a diagnosis."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "What evidence is MOST INCONSISTENT with De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)? Identify the single strongest finding that argues against this diagnosis.", "summary": "The strongest evidence against de novo AML is the absence of other hallmark features like marrow fibrosis or prior myeloproliferative history, but pancytopenia with blasts remains more typical of AML than other alternatives."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of 35% peripheral blasts and pancytopenia (hemoglobin 10 g/dL, platelets 109,000/mm³) strongly support de novo AML (B1.1) over other myeloid or lymphoid malignancies in this subacut…", "summary": "The presence of 35% peripheral blasts and pancytopenia (anemia, thrombocytopenia) in this subacute presentation strongly supports de novo acute myeloid leukemia (AML, B1.1) as the most likely diagnosis. These findings are less consistent with lymphoid malignancies (e.g., ALL, B2) or chronic myelopr…"}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch B1.1 (AML) has posterior 0.493 < 0.75. Dangerous alternative B1.1 (posterior 0.493, danger 0.9) remains unresolved. Further testing (cytogenetics, flow cytometry) is needed to refine differentiation between AML subtypes and MDS/secondary AML."}, "turn_budget_used": 3, "estimated_remaining_value": 2.0, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.49337737276151705, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'pancytopenia', 'Acute myeloid leukemia', 'Myeloid leukemia', 'Multiple myeloma'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.535}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "posterior": 0.493, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 2, "disconfirming": 1, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Pancytopenia and elevated blasts can occur in MDS/secondary AML (B1.3), which has a moderate likelihood in this context…"}, "action_intents": [{"t": 2, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B1.3"]}}
