 subtypes and MDS/secondary AML."}, "turn_budget_used": 4, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.85, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.5162560157063513, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'acute onset', 'Acute myeloid leukemia', 'tics', 'pancytopenia', 'Multiple myeloma', 'onset', 'Myeloid leukemia'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.535}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "posterior": 0.516, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 5, "disconfirming": 1, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Pancytopenia and elevated blasts can occur in MDS/secondary AML (B1.3), which has a moderate likelihood in this context…"}, "action_intents": [{"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B1.3"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=100%, source=primekg]\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal